      "created_at": "2022-07-20T11:33:46.540Z",
      "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/e/e9540093e6b0bf07c5f216ebbf36f93ebfa744e7.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/e9540093e6b0bf07c5f216ebbf36f93ebfa744e7\" title=\"Screenshot_20220719-205856\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e9540093e6b0bf07c5f216ebbf36f93ebfa744e7_2_225x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Screenshot_20220719-205856\" data-base62-sha1=\"xi7dVrbgZ6zPr7Xyiv10MX10Ezt\" width=\"225\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e9540093e6b0bf07c5f216ebbf36f93ebfa744e7_2_225x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e9540093e6b0bf07c5f216ebbf36f93ebfa744e7_2_337x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e9540093e6b0bf07c5f216ebbf36f93ebfa744e7_2_450x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e9540093e6b0bf07c5f216ebbf36f93ebfa744e7_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot_20220719-205856</span><span class=\"informations\">720×1600 95.8 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Remind me again why I like playing Argent Adept?  I mean, he got the job done, but good god the fiddlyness.  Between him and Medico the team was never in more than mild danger, but man was it a long slog to get through around 200 HP (Pouch of Bones twice over) to finally take him low enough that I could ignore the secondary targets and just focus fire to do Gloomy in.  Omnitron U can blow up <em>real</em> good when Second Opinion, Experimental Medicine, Healing Pulse and Regeneration are giving him multiple powers a round.  Oh, you want to hit me for 5, Gloomy?  Go on then, see how well that works out for you.</p>",
